 <details class="risk-guide"><summary>${x("info")} How risk priorities work</summary><div class="risk-guide-grid"><article><span class="priority-pill red">Red · priority check-in</span><p>No sessions in the latest snapshot plus two or more consecutive weekly zero snapshots, attendance in each of the previous three weeks (labelled “Was on target” when they met their weekly target each week, otherwise “Routine broken”), a stop from at least two sessions last week / a prior average of at least two, or no sessions found in any of the last seven weeks (missing weeks count as no session found).</p></article><article><span class="priority-pill yellow">Yellow · personal check-in</span><p>A new zero week with visits in the last 30 days, a drop of at least two sessions from last week or 1.5 below the prior average, or declining Fringe attendance.</p></article><article><span class="priority-pill watch">Watch · monitor</span><p>Still attending, marked Fringe and below their membership target, with no stronger Red or Yellow signal. Unlimited memberships use a target of four sessions.</p></article><article><span class="priority-pill review">Review · missing context</span><p>Zero attendance in a member’s first week, or below-target attendance without the engagement label needed for Watch. Review these cases before choosing an outreach outcome.</p></article></div><p class="risk-guide-note"><strong>Attendance stages:</strong> Early warning = first zero after recent attendance; At risk = two zero snapshots, a sharp stop or declining attendance; Disengaged = 3–4 zero snapshots; Long absence = 5–6; Extended absence = 7+. Monitoring and Needs context describe cases without a confirmed absence stage. Stages use up to eight saved weekly observations. Missing, suspended or ineligible historical slots break the run. Archived weekly summaries are observations, not a verified day-by-day absence record. Existing reports retain their saved history until reimported. Outreach notes and exemptions stay separate.</p><p class="risk-guide-note"><strong>Attendance bands are different:</strong> 0 = Critical; 1 = At Risk; 2 = Low; 3 = Okay; 4+ = Good. Outreach priority also considers history and membership target. The first matching rule wins: Red, then Yellow, then Watch. Missing snapshots stay unknown on the bars. Current suspensions are held out of outreach.</p><p class="risk-guide-note"><strong>Missing history:</strong> When the Attendance history export is included, earlier weeks are counted from actual session dates. Otherwise missing snapshots stay unknown on the bars, but a member with no sessions found in the last seven weeks is still Red. Fringe engagement labels are never invented.</p><p class="risk-guide-note">Imported reports supply these priorities; CSV imports calculate them from the selected cutoff and saved weekly attendance. Team notes change outreach status and temporary exemptions; they do not change the recorded risk category.</p></details>
